      "body": "Implementation candidate accepted for separate final checking.\n\nCandidate: `770f48facb29fe444870a1016538b3ad499954e7`; base: `451aabbafeb4b590aa936b7d5e3e38c306626955`; plan: `1`; issue input: `dddf16fc9a899dbed7d3a32eddde7dc124c6cbe8f1883749d4864515e2f69c88`.\n\nIndependent work-unit checker accepted the exact candidate under plan1: four Linux Debug/Release exception OFF/ON suites each passed119/119 (476 unique tests), with28 controller cases repeated3 times per configuration (336 executions). All16 Python groups,138 methods,103 scenarios, exact-union verifier and metadata validation passed. The unchanged Debug baseline returns0 for E5/E6 while candidate returns1; the baseline-header caller passes against candidate libraries. Native Windows execution was explicitly waived and remains unverified; both implementations and registration were reviewed. Release malformed-input parser rejection still returns0 with parse failure/skip1, completion0 and worker deaths0; this separate policy limitation is not successful required replay. Null-device/controlled-worker evidence makes no real-driver, cache, durability or general binary ABI claim. Separate fresh final checking is still required; the issue remains open pending merge.\n\nPrepared source comparison (branch will be published with the implementation PR): https://github.com/robinwassen/Fossilize/compare/master...codex/issue-13-retain-child-loss\n\n<!-- harness-ready:issue13-20261030:5b9113479172fb37d9cc844e31a68238aa5baea2b1e59d20908b316dd89d8ed5 -->\n\n<!-- fossilize-migration-v1:readiness-2e6af7010eb504b0e458dd71638e60be3237f4477847b4de5e450abe6cfb27a3 -->\n",
